    <statement><p>Find a parametrization, using <m>\cos(t)</m> and <m>\sin(t)</m>, of the following curve:</p>
<p>The intersection of the plane <m>y=5</m> with the sphere <m>x^2+y^2+z^2=50</m></p>
<p><m>\bf r\it (t)=\langle</m>
  <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,
  <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_1"/>,
  <fillin characters="20" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_2"/>
<m>\rangle</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right);\,5;\,5\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>y=5</m> in the equation of the sphere gives:



<me>x^2+\left(5\right)^2+z^2=50 \Rightarrow x^2+z^2=25</me>
This circle in the horizontal plane <m>y=5</m> has the parametrization 


<m>x = \sqrt{25}\cos t, z=\sqrt{25}\sin t</m>.Therefore, the points on the intersection of the plane 


<m>y=5</m> and the sphere <m>x^2+y^2+z^2=50</m>, can be written in the form 
<m>\left(5\cos t,5,5\sin t\right)</m>, yielding the following parametrization:



<me>\bf r\it (t)=\left\lt 5\cos t,5,5\sin t\right&gt;</me>



</solution>
